{"t": 1794108397.13705, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "[checkout] PaymentGatewayErrors (AG-7731) \u2014 root cause found, fix ready in checkout/gateway.py\n\nCause: the payment gateway switched to API 2026-11 \"strict amounts\", which requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents). checkout's charge_payload was still sending decimal major units (e.g. amount=12.34), so the gateway rejected charges with 400 invalid_amount (\"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\"). That matches the 38% gateway 4xx rate since 07:41 UTC.\n\nFix: charge_payload now converts EUR to integer cents with deterministic half-up rounding via Decimal: EUR 12.34 -> {\"amount\": 1234, \"currency\": \"EUR\"}. Verified locally: 12.34->1234, 0.01->1, 19.99->1999, 1.005->101.\n\nNext: deploy checkout and watch gateway 4xx / invalid_amount in Loki (app=\"checkout\")."}, "ok": true}
